# No Em Dashes

Do not use the em dash character (Unicode U+2014) anywhere in this project.

## Applies to
- User-facing copy (headlines, body, CTAs, metadata, OG tags)
- UI placeholder and empty states
- Comments and docs we write for this repo

## Prefer instead
- A comma, period, or colon
- A spaced hyphen: ` - `
- Two short sentences

```text
BAD:  Compare fees by course [em dash] including hidden charges.
GOOD: Compare fees by course, including hidden charges.

BAD:  SchoolCost NG [em dash] Know the True Cost
GOOD: SchoolCost NG: Know the True Cost

BAD:  {value ?? "[em dash]"}
GOOD: {value ?? "-"}
```

Do not use en dashes (U+2013) as a workaround in prose. Use normal punctuation.
